## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## A crash dump is a developer's artifact, and this binary runs in someone
## else's project directory. Without this, a virtual machine crash writes a
## multi-megabyte `erl_crash.dump` next to their source files, which is both
## noise and a file they did not ask for. Zero means the runtime does not
## attempt to write one at all.
-env ERL_CRASH_DUMP_SECONDS 0
